From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Agent <claude-agent@invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:11:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] clutter/color: Give parametric color states a target color
 volume
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A parametric color state only described its encoding: primaries,
transfer function and the primary color volume's luminances. Add the
target color volume its content was prepared for, as
wp_image_description_creator_params_v1 declares it: mastering display
primaries, mastering luminance range (SMPTE ST 2086), and the maximum
content and frame-average light levels (CTA-861-H).

It is held privately in ClutterColorStateParams, as
ClutterColorTargetVolume from the uninstalled
clutter-color-state-params-private.h; the public ClutterLuminance and
the other installed structures are unchanged. Undeclared parts are
absent (has_primaries and has_luminance FALSE, max_cll and max_fall 0);
luminances are in the units of the state's own ClutterLuminance.
Additive API, exported for libmutter (which creates states from client
input) and listed in the symbols file:

 - clutter_color_state_params_new_with_target_volume(): a copy of a
   parametric state with the given target volume, validated by the
   caller.
 - clutter_color_state_params_get_target_volume().
 - clutter_color_state_params_get_peak_headroom(): the content's range
   as multiples of its reference white, which every conversion
   anchors. The effective peak is the smallest of MaxCLL (if declared),
   the target maximum luminance (if declared) and, for an encoding
   whose signal range bounds it, the encoding's maximum, the larger of
   its nominal and extended maximum. Without any declaration it is the
   encoding maximum, 10000 cd/m² for PQ; MaxFALL, an average, never
   lowers it. Extended-range linear encodings (ext_linear, scRGB-style
   content) give meaning to values above 1.0, so their nominal maximum
   bounds nothing: their peak is the smaller of MaxCLL and the target
   maximum, whichever are declared, and with neither it is unknown and
   the function returns FALSE. This is the single definition of the
   effective peak.

The target volume takes part in equality and hashing. It is compared
exactly, unlike the encoding luminances: its values are declarations,
not derived, and a different declaration is a different state. So the
color transform cache, keyed by state equality, tells such states
apart.

Equality is also what decided whether a transform needs any
operation. Two states that differ only in their target volume encode
pixels identically, and treating them as different would have added
an EOTF, two matrices and an inverse EOTF to an identity conversion,
which also blocks direct scanout. The transform now builds a pipeline
only when the encodings differ, using the new internal
clutter_color_state_encoding_equals(), which is equality without the
target volume. Nothing renders the target volume yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DLZiLBYev72J1s4D37L7Bi
